{0 Type theory of the CommonMark AST}

@llm_generated true

{1 Goal}

The {!Oymarkit_.Block} type admits values that the CommonMark
parser will never produce. For example, the AST permits a [Blocks]
splicing node nested inside another [Blocks] node, or a [Heading]
whose [level] field is [42]. The parser produces a strict subset of
[Block.t]; we call this subset the {e well-typed} ASTs.

Our goal is to characterize that subset {b empirically} — by
generating broadly, running a battery of properties, shrinking each
counterexample, and promoting each shrunk witness into a typing rule.

The discipline that emerges is the type theory of the CommonMark AST
as observed through this implementation.

{1 Why "type theory"?}

The CommonMark specification is operational: it defines a parser, not a
grammar over the AST. The AST type {!Oymarkit_.Block.t} is therefore
permissive — it admits "ill-typed" values that no parse can produce.

A typing discipline carves out the well-typed subset. Three places it
can live:

{ol
{- {b In the type.} Refine constructors (e.g. [Heading] could carry a
   [level : (int, 1..6) refinement]). OCaml's surface syntax limits us.}
{- {b In a generator.} The shape of the generator is the type discipline
   made syntactic — every constraint in a generator override is a rule.}
{- {b In a predicate table.} Named, declarative checks lifted over the
   tree. Useful for {e reporting} which rule was violated.}}

We use all three. The surface AST {!Oymarkit_property.Gen_block.s_block}
is (1), [gen_block] is (2), and [Rule.all] is (3).

{1 Architecture}

{[
                Gen_block.gen_block
                       |
                       v
                Gen_block.s_block
                       |
                       | Gen_block.to_block
                       v
                Oymarkit_.Block.t
                       |
                       v
                Property.{roundtrip, uniformity_*, ...}
                       |
                       v
                Pass | Fail { reason; expected; actual }
]}

The pipeline has four components, in [src/property/]:

{ul
{- {!Oymarkit_property.Gen_block.s_block} — a narrow surface AST that
   {e cannot express} most rule violations by construction.}
{- {!Oymarkit_property.Gen_block.gen_block} — a [QCheck2.Gen.t] over
   [s_block]. Size-bounded with integrated tree-shrinking.}
{- {!Oymarkit_property.Gen_block.to_block} — lowers [s_block] into
   [Oymarkit_.Block.t] using smart constructors.}
{- {!Oymarkit_property.Property.all} — the property battery
   ([roundtrip], [normalize_idempotent], [render_determinism],
   [uniformity_block_quote], [uniformity_list_item]).}}

{1 Workflow}

The loop is:

{ol
{- {b Generate.} Sample an [s_block] from the current [gen_block].
   The generator's current shape is the conjectured typing discipline.}
{- {b Lower.} Apply [to_block] to obtain a [Block.t].}
{- {b Check.} Run every [Property.t] in [Property.all] on the block.}
{- {b Shrink.} On any failure, QCheck2 shrinks the [s_block] to a
   minimal counterexample (integrated shrinking — no separate
   shrinker to maintain).}
{- {b Diagnose.} Read the shrunk witness; identify the
   typing rule it violates. Examples we expect to see:
   {ul
   {- A paragraph beginning with [- ] inside a list item reparses
     as a nested list.}
   {- A thematic break of [-] characters inside a [Ulist] item
     collides with the list marker.}
   {- A code block whose info string contains spaces.}}}
{- {b Promote.} Encode the rule in one of three places:
   {ul
   {- Tighten the surface AST (e.g. add a [Para_safe] variant that
     forbids container-marker prefixes).}
   {- Tighten the generator (e.g. reject paragraphs starting with [- ]).}
   {- Add a named entry to [Rule.all] so future failures can be
     {e labelled} with which rule they violate.}}}
{- {b Repeat} until [Property.all] holds at large [count]. The
   surviving set of rules {b is} the typing discipline.}}

{1 What "equal" means}

[Property.canonical] is the equality used by every check.

It is currently {!Oymarkit_.Pp.pp_block} applied to the
{{!Oymarkit_.Block.normalize}normalized} block. Two blocks are equal
iff their canonical forms are equal strings.

This is deliberately lossy: it drops [Meta.t], drops most
[Layout] fields, and truncates inline previews. The {e right} granularity
for discovering structural rules; the {e wrong} granularity for
layout-preservation bugs. Sharpen when needed.

{1 The current rule table}

See {!Oymarkit_property.Gen_block.Rule.all}. As of the initial
scaffold, it lists only the rules already enforced by the generator
shape:

{ul
{- [heading_level_in_range] — [1 <= level <= 6].}
{- [paragraph_nonempty] — paragraphs have at least one inline.}
{- [list_items_nonempty] — lists and items are non-empty.}
{- [block_quote_nonempty] — block quote bodies are non-empty.}}

These are placeholders. The interesting rules will be added as
counterexamples are discovered.

{1 What this is not}

{ul
{- {b A spec.} The discovered rules are this implementation's behavior,
   not the CommonMark spec. They are likely a superset of any clean
   formal characterization.}
{- {b A round-trip fixer.} When a counterexample shows that
   [parse (render b) ≠ b], the rule we add says "don't generate
   such [b]" — we do not change the parser or renderer to make it
   round-trip.}
{- {b Exhaustive.} The surface AST is intentionally narrow. Extensions
   (math, tables, footnotes), HTML, links, and setext headings are
   omitted from v1 and will be added once the core is stable.}}

{1 Open directions}

{ul
{- {b Sharper equality.} A structural [Block.equal_ignoring_meta] that
   does not go through [Pp]'s lossy preview.}
{- {b Inline-level properties.} Currently only block-level
   round-tripping is checked. Inline-level analogues should follow.}
{- {b Container battery.} [uniformity_*] is currently defined for
   block quote and unordered list. Add ordered list, nested
   containers, and an [n]-deep wrapping variant.}
{- {b Rule provenance.} Each shrunk counterexample should be recorded
   with the rule it gave rise to, so the rule table doubles as a
   regression suite of minimal witnesses.}}
